  "2026-08-13T12:32:12.719Z","harness:codex","Post-merge continuation: npm outdated newly reported compatible jscpd 5.0.15 after PR #996 had already merged. All-status searches for the exact version and quality-gate refresh found no version-specific item; this canonical same-day tooling item is reopened rather than duplicating lineage. Only this item is in progress."
  "2026-08-13T12:33:27.529Z","harness:codex","Supply-chain evidence: jscpd 5.0.15 was published at 2026-08-13T11:54:56Z from gitHead 10540cbb8e2b984bd8381719df99aa45e3bc397b with npm SLSA provenance and matching registry integrity. npm audit signatures verified all 557 package signatures and 203 attestations. The explicit minimumReleaseAge exclusions cover only jscpd 5.0.15 and its six platform packages."
  "2026-08-13T12:45:44.797Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: focused ESLint, typecheck, audit, and jscpd duplicate detection passed; jscpd 5.0.15 scanned 987 files with zero clones or duplicated lines/tokens. Full sandboxed coverage passed 490/490 files and 7256/7256 tests at exact 100% statements (52698/52698), branches (38711/38711), functions (10832/10832), and lines (50910/50910). The aggregate pnpm lint run passed its strict static, docstring, duplicate, package-boundary, parity, assurance, security, and context gates, then one ./sdk/governance median sample measured 264ms against 248ms under concurrent host load; the immediate standalone median-of-five SDK entrypoint gate passed every unchanged budget, so the aggregate run is recorded as partial rather than relabeled green."
  "2026-08-13T12:51:30.467Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: the packed artifact gate passed (1390 files, no forbidden source maps); a fresh temporary packed npx installation passed at 2026.8.13 across all 13 packages; and package-first dogfood completed 88 commands in an isolated /tmp project with lifecycle, packages, scaffold typecheck, upgrade, and linked-test execution all successful. Semantic dogfood was explicitly not attempted because PM_DOGFOOD_SEMANTIC was unset and is not counted as acceptance."
